      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T10:42:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks! I switched to watching xyz.openbmc_project.Software.ActivationBlocksTransition via GetSubTreePaths and made the wait event-driven off InterfacesRemoved rather than polling, which avoids a sync bus.call() on the async bus.\n\nTo clarify on preventing new updates: this logic defers past active updates up to a timeout rather than rejecting them. Whether we need a full interlock is noted as an open option in the commit message.\n\nI looked into using the existing systemd reboot-guard unit instead, but skipped it because it isn\u0027t ref-counted (one finished update disarms it for all), the BMC updater disarms it prior to self-reboot, and blocked reboots fail instead of retrying. Using ActivationBlocksTransition felt like the cleanest route, though I\u0027m open to moving the check into a shared \"update in progress\" view if preferred.",
      "parentUuid": "f31f225a_43823b74",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 1,
