      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T13:11:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right — this patch only defers past the updates already in progress (timeout-bounded); it doesn\u0027t stop a new VR/CPLD update from starting during the wait. Preventing that needs a shared \"BMC reboot pending\" state every updater checks before starting — a cross-updater interlock that doesn\u0027t exist today. Options: (1) add that interlock (stack-wide change), (2) reject a BMC Immediate update while other updates are active (no wait window; reboot later when idle), or\n(3) treat defer+timeout as best-effort (this patch). Given the interlock is a bigger design, I lean toward (2) as the smaller, race-free option — but happy to follow your preference.",
      "parentUuid": "607c8807_251245e8",
